==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|inter|twine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɪntə(ɹ)ˈtwaɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-intertwine.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪn|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[twine#Verb|twine]] ([[thing]]s) together.
##: {{synonyms|en|entwine}}
##: {{coordinate terms|en|interweave|tangle}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=w:Plato|title=Sophist|translator=Lesley Brown|page=240c|passage=''You see, no doubt, that yet again, thanks to this '''intertwining''', our many-headed sophist has forced us against our will to admit that what is not is in a way.''}}
## To [[connect#Verb|connect]] (things) [[closely]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## To [[become]] twined together.
## {{lb|en|figurative}} To become [[mutually]] [[involve]]d.

